# What ships is: out/src/** (the compiled extension), media/** (the activity bar
# icon and the task view's stylesheet and client script), package.json,
# README.md, CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE and icon.png. Everything below is build- or
# development-time only.
#
# media/ is deliberately NOT excluded. The webview loads its stylesheet and
# script from there through `asWebviewUri`, and the activity bar icon is
# referenced from `contributes.viewsContainers` — so excluding it would produce a
# VSIX whose UI is a blank panel with no icon.
#
# Nothing here is required at runtime. The extension has zero runtime
# dependencies, reads its configuration from VS Code settings, and keeps
# credentials in SecretStorage — so there is no data file, no .env and no
# node_modules to carry.

.git/**
.github/**
.gitignore
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**

# TypeScript sources and the test suite. The compiled output in out/src is what
# runs; shipping the sources again would roughly double the package for no
# runtime benefit.
src/**
test/**
out/test/**
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.build.json
**/*.ts
**/*.map

# Dependency tree. Packaged with --no-dependencies because devDependencies are
# the only dependencies; this is belt and braces.
node_modules/**
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# Research, audit and release material. Useful in the repository, noise in the VSIX.
docs/**
PUBLISHING.md

# Never package secrets or local environment files, whatever else changes here.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Build artefacts
*.vsix
coverage/**
*.log
.DS_Store
